    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a2">

                <pb facs="0258" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv05/pg248"/>

                <head>Appendix II to IC–176F</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d22-f1"
                    /></seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-25">April 25, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Marquis Saionji to the President of
                        the Peace Conference</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clemenceau</hi>)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>: The Chiefs of Government of the
                    Great Powers having already heard the Delegates of China on the subject of the
                    question of the Province of Shantung, I wish to express in the name of the
                    Japanese Delegation, the desire to see as soon as possible a further meeting to
                    expedite the definitive settlement of this question.</p>
                <p>Considering the peculiar importance of this question for Japan, I would be
                    grateful, Mr. President, if you would keep us, so far as possible, informed of
                    all steps in its furtherance.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Saionji</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
